1536	1687	1533	1533	he	-1	' sheep 's kidneys is good , uncommon good , if they do them without burning . But I be so galled in the saddle ten days , and never a comely meal of it . And when they hear “ King 's service ” cried , they give me the worst of everything . All the way down from London , I had a rogue of a fellow in front of me , eating the fat of the land before me , and every one bowing down to him . He could go three miles to my one though he never changed his horse . He might have robbed me at any minute , if I had been worth the trouble . A red mare he rideth , strong in the loins , and pointed quite small in the head . I shall live to see him hanged yet . '
